                <pb facs="1172" n="1040" xml:id="pg1040"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.05/83: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-12-29T09:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 29,
                                1926—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 29—6:03
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>645. My telegram number 641, December 27, 4 p.m. At a meeting of interested
                    Ministers yesterday afternoon Italian Minister was persuaded to make possible
                    the necessary unanimity with regard to rendition of the Mixed Court by acceding
                    to compromise proposal suggested by the consular body at Shanghai with respect
                    to the selection of senior consul’s deputies. It is therefore expected rendition
                    can be effected January 1st.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
